# 1. What the object is

Think of each concept as a reusable node:

```txt
Concept
  ├── name
  ├── aliases
  ├── description
  ├── deeper explanation
  ├── related texts
  ├── related artworks
  ├── animation prompts
  ├── related concepts
  ├── usage history in essays/videos
```

Example:

```txt
Concept: Ouroboros

Meaning:
The serpent eating its own tail; self-reflexivity, cyclicality, totality, self-renewal.

Visual motifs:
Circular serpent
Cosmic egg
Solar/lunar symbolism
Encircling world
Black/white duality

Related concepts:
Mercurius
Prima materia
Conjunction
World soul
Eternity

Related art:
Rosarium Philosophorum plates
Theatrum Chemicum imagery
Alchemical manuscript diagrams

Animation ideas:
Slow breathing ring
Serpent subtly moving
Tail bite glowing
Circle enclosing stars
```

That is gold.

---

# 2. Why this is powerful

Because then the visual system becomes **grounded**.

Instead of asking:

```txt
Find some mystical image
```

the engine can say:

```txt
This section is about conjunction.
Pull 3 approved conjunction artworks from the glossary corpus.
Prefer 16th–17th century manuscript or engraving style.
Use the animated variant if available.
```

That is far more coherent.

It also means the glossary page on the site becomes useful in its own right.

You’re not just building a backend asset library.
You’re building a **visual-symbolic atlas**.

